//! IR-Diff — semantic comparison of LLVM IR text files.
//!
//! This module powers the `tml ir-diff` CLI command. It parses LLVM IR text
//! into a structured representation, normalizes register and label names so
//! that two semantically equivalent IR files compare equal, and produces a
//! structured diff result for any remaining differences.
//!
//! Used by the self-hosting effort (phase12d) to verify parity between the
//! C++ frontend and TML-implemented stages.
//!
//! # Submodules
//!
//! | Module | Description |
//! |--------|-------------|
//! | [`types`] | Shared data types (IrModule, IrFunction, IrBlock, IrInstr, ParseError) |
//! | [`parser`] | LLVM IR text parser |
//! | [`normalizer`] | Canonical register and label renaming pass |
//! | [`differ`] | Semantic comparison of two normalized IR modules |

pub mod types
pub mod parser
pub mod normalizer
pub mod differ
